### Page 6 of 12

```text
Cheyenne Junior League Complex Scoreboard & Sound System
2021/2022 Cheyenne Community Public Recreation District Grant Application
Submitted by City of Cheyenne, Community Recreation and Events Department

The Cheyenne Junior League Athletic Complex is a 30-acre sports facility with nine fully
operational softball and baseball fields. Every year, the CJL Complex which is located at Dell
Range Boulevard and Converse Avenue registers almost 600 boys and girls, ages 5-12, to
participate on one of the 40 youth teams across four divisional age groups. WYCO Baseball,
WYCO Softball, Cheyenne Mustangs, and Extreme Girls Softball call the CJL Complex home.
Management is anticipating a 10 percent increase in registrations by next year which will
necessitate ten additional teams for a total of 700 players. In addition to these youth leagues, the
CJL Complex also hosts Laramie County School District 1’s High School Girls Softball program,
providing practice and competition facilities for another 135 athletes.
The City is in need of digital scoreboards and distributed speaker audio systems to enhance
engagement and the overall player and participant experience.

The CJL Athletic Complex Storage Shed project will provide a necessary component to the support
infrastructure with the installation electronic scoreboards and distributed speaker audio systems in
three of the fields. Bid information was used as source documents for the project budget.
If awarded, the project will immediately go through the City of Cheyenne’s bidding process so
that work, weather permitting, will be completed by Fall 2021. Grant funds will purchase three
electronic scoreboards and all necessary components for the distributed speaker audio systems.

Anticipated usage for the CJL Complex between youth sports and the Laramie County School
District 1 could reach 1,000 athletes within the next year or two. The scoreboards and sound
systems will be utilized by spectators, athletes, coaches, volunteers, city staff, and other support
staff who utilize the three fields.

Grant Request:  $100,000

Project Need
Proposed Resolution
Project Beneficiaries
Project Budget
